      "content": "That statement works for a first pass, but I'm worried about the \"technical glitch\" phrasing. If journalists start digging into the logs, they'll see that names and emails were actually exported from the database. \n\nIf we say \"no sensitive information was compromised\" and then it comes out later that 5,000 customer records were leaked, we're dead. Are you absolutely sure we can stand by the claim that no sensitive info was taken? Can we frame it so we're being truthful without actually admitting the leak happened?",
